# Gitignored files copied into every worktree Claude Code creates — `--worktree`, a
# subagent with `isolation: worktree`, and parallel sessions in the desktop app.
# .gitignore syntax; only files that match *and* are gitignored are copied.
#
# The test for belonging here is: gitignored, and **not reconstructible from a command**.
# Almost nothing passes it, which is the point — a worktree that silently carries state
# the main checkout has is a worktree that passes tests the branch would fail.

# The cutscene's reference audio track. A local copy of copyrighted music that must never
# enter the repository, and that no command can fetch — so a worktree doing cutscene work
# has no way to get it back. `CutsceneOverlay` discovers it at this path when present and
# plays without it when not, so its absence is silent rather than a failure.
apps/game/public/tng-intro.*

# Local vite / wrangler environment overrides, if any exist.
.env
.env.local
*.local

# Deliberately NOT here:
#
#   node_modules/  — pnpm's is a symlink farm into .pnpm; copying dereferences the links
#                    into ~640 MB per worktree. `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
#                    --prefer-offline` rebuilds it from the machine-global store in ~3s,
#                    which .claude/hooks/session-start.sh does automatically for a session
#                    and every worktree subagent is told to run first.
#   .data/         — 34 MB of raw HYG downloads that exist only to produce
#                    data/catalog (committed). `pnpm catalog:fetch` re-downloads them.
#   apps/server/.wrangler/ — local Worker state; a fresh one is correct.
